{
  "page": 8,
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Benchmarks. We compare RESPO with the baselines in a diverse suite of safety environments. We",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        75.08882141113281,
        503.9951477050781,
        84.11493682861328
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "consider high-dimensional environments in Safety Gym [30] (namely PointButton and CarGoal),",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        86.11737060546875,
        505.2450866699219,
        95.02393341064453
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Safety PyBullet [50] (namely DroneCircle and BallRun), and Safety MuJoCo [51], (namely Safety",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        97.0263671875,
        504.3453369140625,
        105.93292999267578
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "HalfCheetah and Reacher). We also show our algorithm in a multi-drone environment with multiple",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        107.93536376953125,
        504.0007019042969,
        116.84192657470703
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "hard and soft constraints. More detailed experiment explanations and evaluations are in the appendix.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        118.8443603515625,
        505.7464599609375,
        127.75092315673828
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "6.1",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        142.8958282470703,
        120.4532470703125,
        151.85220336914062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Main Experiments in Safety Gym, Safety PyBullet, and MuJoCo",
      "bbox": [
        130.4158477783203,
        142.8958282470703,
        404.2379150390625,
        151.85220336914062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We compare our algorithm with SOTA benchmarks on various high-dimensional (up to 76D observa-",
      "bbox": [
        107.53199768066406,
        162.83094787597656,
        505.6579895019531,
        171.89691162109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tion space), complex environments in the stochastic setting, i.e., where the environment and/or policy",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        173.89935302734375,
        504.3470153808594,
        182.805908203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "are stochastic. Particularly, we examine environments in Safety Gym, Safety PyBullet, and Safety",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        184.808349609375,
        504.3465881347656,
        193.71490478515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "MuJoCo. The environments provide reward for achieving a goal behavior or location, while the cost",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        195.71734619140625,
        503.9974365234375,
        204.6239013671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is based on tangible (e.g., avoiding quickly moving objects) and non-tangible (e.g., satisfying speed",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        206.6263427734375,
        503.995849609375,
        215.53289794921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "limit) constraints. Environments like PointButton require intricate behavior where specific buttons",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        217.53533935546875,
        504.00433349609375,
        226.44189453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "must be reached while avoiding multiple moving obstacles, stationary hazards, and wrong buttons.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        228.4443359375,
        500.4566345214844,
        237.35089111328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Overall, RESPO achieves the best balance between optimizing reward and minimizing cost violations",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        244.7138214111328,
        503.9960021972656,
        253.73992919921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "across all the environments. Specifically, our approach generally has the highest reward performance",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        255.74237060546875,
        504.0006408691406,
        264.64892578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(see the red lines from the top row of Figure 2) among the safety-constrained algorithms while",
      "bbox": [
        107.6709976196289,
        266.6513671875,
        504.00384521484375,
        275.55792236328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "maintaining reasonably low to 0 cost violations (like in HalfCheetah). When RESPO performs the",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        277.4009704589844,
        503.9967346191406,
        286.4669189453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "second highest, the highest-performing safety algorithm always incurs several times more violations",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        288.4693603515625,
        503.9975280761719,
        297.37591552734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "than RESPO – for instance, RCRL in PointButton or PPOLag in Drone Circle. Non-primal-dual",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        299.2587890625,
        503.9970397949219,
        308.284912109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CMDP approaches, namely CRPO, P3O, and PCPO generally satisfy their cost threshold constraints,",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        310.1687927246094,
        505.2432556152344,
        319.1949157714844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "but their reward performances rarely exceed that of PPOLag. RCRL generally has extremes of high",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        321.0777893066406,
        503.99951171875,
        330.1039123535156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "reward and high cost, like in BallRun, or low reward and low cost, like in CarGoal. FAC and CBF",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        331.9867858886719,
        504.3092346191406,
        341.0129089355469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "generally have conservative behavior that sacrifices reward performance to minimize cost.",
