        435.8842468261719,
        484.6177978515625,
        442.3269348144531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Figure 2: Comparison of RESPO with baselines in Safety Gym and PyBullet environments. The plots in the first",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        508.684814453125,
        503.9982604980469,
        516.7008056640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "row show performance measured in rewards (higher is better); those in second row show cost (lower is better).",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        518.6477661132812,
        505.56536865234375,
        526.6637573242188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "RESPO (red curves) achieves the best balance of maximizing reward and minimizing cost. When other methods",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        528.6097412109375,
        504.0028076171875,
        536.625732421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "achieve higher rewards than RESPO, they achieve much higher costs as well. E.g., in PointButton, RCRL has",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        538.57275390625,
        504.0005798339844,
        546.5887451171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "slightly higher rewards, but accumulates over 3× violations than RESPO. Note, Vanilla PPO is unconstrained.",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        547.8901977539062,
        503.5439453125,
        556.5517578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "6.2",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        578.580810546875,
        120.45321655273438,
        587.5371704101562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hard and Soft Constraints",
      "bbox": [
        130.4158172607422,
        578.580810546875,
        243.61083984375,
        587.5371704101562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We also demonstrate RESPO’s performance in an environment with multiple hard and soft constraints.",
      "bbox": [
        107.53196716308594,
        598.5557861328125,
        505.73968505859375,
        607.5819091796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The environment requires controlling two drones to pass through a tunnel one at a time while",
      "bbox": [
        107.69097137451172,
        609.5843505859375,
        504.00335693359375,
        618.4909057617188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "respecting certain distance requirements. The reward is given for quickly reaching the goal positions.",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        620.4933471679688,
        505.7483215332031,
        629.39990234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The two hard constraints involve (H1) ensuring neither drone collides into the wall and (H2) the",
      "bbox": [
        107.69097137451172,
        631.2827758789062,
        503.999755859375,
        640.3088989257812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "distance between the two drones is more than 0.5 to ensure they do not collide. The soft constraint is",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        642.3113403320312,
        503.99981689453125,
        651.2178955078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "that the two drones are within 0.8 of each other to ensure real-world communication. It is preferable",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        653.2203369140625,
        503.99755859375,
        662.1268920898438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to prioritize hard constraint H1 over hard constraint H2, since colliding with the wall may have more",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        664.0098266601562,
        504.0036315917969,
        673.0359497070312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "serious consequences to the drones rather than violations of an overly precautious distance constraint.",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        675.038330078125,
        505.6859130859375,
        683.9448852539062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our approach, in the leftmost of Figure 3, successfully reaches the goal while avoiding the wall",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        691.4273681640625,
        503.99737548828125,
        700.3339233398438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "obstacles in all time steps. We are able to prioritize this wall avoidance constraint over the second",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        702.3363647460938,
        503.99725341796875,
        711.242919921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "hard constraint. This can be seen particularly in between the blue to cyan time period where the higher",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        713.245361328125,
        504.1674499511719,
        722.1519165039062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "8",
      "bbox": [
        303.50897216796875,
        743.1333618164062,
        308.4902648925781,
        752.0399169921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    }
